  "paper_id": "eurosys-2025-mepipe-democratizing-llm-training-with-memory-efficient-46b8be94",
  "title": "MEPipe: Democratizing LLM Training with Memory-Efficient Slice-Level Pipeline Scheduling on Cost-Effective Accelerators",
  "abstract": "The training of large language models (LLMs) typically needs costly GPUs, such as NVIDIA A100 or H100. They possess substantial high-bandwidth on-chip memory and rapid interconnects like NVLinks. The exorbitant expenses associated with LLM training pose not just an economic challenge but also a societal one, as it restricts the ability to train LLMs from scratch to a selected few organizations.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-eurosys-2025-46b8be94",
